      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lacona was laid out in 1856 and formally incorporated in 1881, marking its official emergence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lacona%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The arrival of the Chariton, Des Moines & Southern Railroad in late 1878 gave Lacona direct rail access, boosting local commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lacona_iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 20th century, Lacona shifted from diverse farming to mechanized row‑crop production of corn and soybeans, spurred by post‑WWI tractor technology.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lacona_iowa",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Willis Cabin, built in 1846 by the Willis family, now stands in Lacona as a restored pioneer log‑cabin museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lacona_iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Settlers from the Willis family began homesteading along White Breast Creek in 1846, laying the groundwork for what would become Lacona.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
